The MIT licence above covers the code and teaching material in this repository,
with the following exceptions.

### notebooks/voronoi.py -- voronoi_finite_polygons_2d()

That single function is adapted from a Stack Overflow answer posted in 2013
(https://stackoverflow.com/a/20678647) and is therefore available under
**CC BY-SA 3.0** (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/), not MIT.
Attribution is retained in the function's docstring. If you reuse that function,
CC BY-SA 3.0's share-alike condition applies to it; the rest of the file and the
rest of this repository remain MIT.

### Datasets

No dataset in this repository is covered by this licence. The Atera data is
